---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About — Emmanuel Akanmu" dim={true}>
  <article class="wrap page">
    <p class="eyebrow">about</p>
    <h1>The origin story</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Software engineer at Walmart Global Tech. I build production AI systems
        for infrastructure operations and user-owned intelligence.
      </p>

      <h2>Selected impact at Walmart</h2>
      <p>
        I designed and shipped the integration and orchestration layer for an AI
        first responder spanning four enterprise systems. Decomposing it into
        independently testable subagents supported incremental delivery and reduced
        context assembly from roughly 15 minutes to under two.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also analyzed 454 production incidents across infrastructure supporting
        tens of thousands of virtual-machine hosts, identified 160 automation
        candidates across six categories, and ranked seven opportunities by value,
        effort, and delivery risk.
      </p>
      <p>
        I evaluated three AI platforms against seven operational use cases and
        strengthened the resulting roadmap through a ten-issue review of data
        integrity, safety, governance, and measurement.
      </p>

      <h2>Technical focus</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>AI systems:</strong> LangGraph, MCP, ReAct agents, tool orchestration, grounded retrieval, and evaluation</li>
        <li><strong>Software:</strong> Python, TypeScript/JavaScript, FastAPI, React, Next.js, Node.js, PostgreSQL, and REST APIs</li>
        <li><strong>Infrastructure and operations:</strong> Kubernetes, Docker, infrastructure automation, service orchestration, incident response, root-cause analysis, operational data analysis, and AI safety and governance</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        What I care about is where this is going. AI, robotics, the climb toward AGI
        and whatever comes after. I'm curious how far it goes, and I want to be in the
        room where it actually happens: a frontier AI lab, or a top-tier company
        that's building and evolving these models, not just using them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Here's what I believe. Intelligence is the highest-leverage asset a human
        being has. Applied, compounded, and stacked over time, it beats everything
        else. That's the bet I'm making with my own.
      </p>
      <p>
        The goal is simple. Use that intelligence to build systems that make life
        better. Make everything easier. Make life fun. Systems that matter, and a life
        I designed on purpose.
      </p>

      <p class="resume-cta">
        <a class="resume-link" href="/emmanuel-akanmu-resume.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          View résumé (PDF) →
        </a>
      </p>

      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/fallennyx">GitHub</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/emmanuelakanmu/">LinkedIn</a></li>
        <li><a href="/emmanuel-akanmu-resume.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Résumé</a></li>
        <li><a href="mailto:1eakanmu@gmail.com">Email</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-top: 3rem; }
  .page h1 { font-size: clamp(34px, 7vw, 52px); color: #fff; margin: 14px 0 2rem; }
  .resume-cta { margin: 1.75rem 0 0; }
  .resume-link {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: background 0.2s ease, color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .resume-link:hover {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #000;
  }
</style>
